# Frontend (Next.js). Copy to .env.local (git-ignored: never commit it).
#
# Everything called NEXT_PUBLIC_ is written into the page every visitor downloads: it is PUBLIC. Put an address or an ID there, never a
# key, a secret, a token or a password. (Secrets belong to the backend: see TokenLaunchpad-be/apps/*/.env.example.)

# --- Public: the backend ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The API. Sessions are cookies, so it has to be an origin the API lists in its CORS_ORIGINS.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
# The live-updates server, if it is not the API itself.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=

# --- Public: the chain and wallets ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The RPC the browser reads the chain through, and the embedded wallet looks accounts up on. Use your own (Alchemy, Infura) and restrict its
# key to your domain: anyone can read it in the page.
NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=
# Privy's App ID: public by design. Leave it out and the app is the plain wallet app (MetaMask, Phantom); with it, Google and email work too.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=
# WalletConnect's project ID: public by design. Leave it out to turn WalletConnect off.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
# A faucet to send people to when their wallet has no testnet ETH.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FAUCET_URL=
# Hosts token images may load from, comma separated (the page's Content-Security-Policy allows only these). The IPFS gateway.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGE_ORIGINS=https://ipfs.io

# --- Build time (not shipped to the browser) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Which TokenLaunchpad-be/packages/deployments/<name>.json the build takes the launchpad's addresses from.
DEPLOYMENT=local
# The folder the app is built into. The demo uses its own (.next-demo) so a test build cannot overwrite the files it serves.
# NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next
